{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Oh Danny [G]boy, the pipes, the [C]pipes are [G]calling
From glen to [G]glen, and [Em]down the [Am]mountain [D]side,
The summer's [G]gone, and [G7]all the [C]roses [Am]falling,
'Tis [G]you, 'tis [Em]you must [Am]go and I must [D]bide.
But come ye [G]back when [C]summer's in the [G]meadow,
Or when the [Em]valley's [Am]hushed and [D]white with snow,
'Tis I'll be [G]here in [C]sunshine [G]or in [Em]shadow,
Oh Danny [G]boy, oh [Em]Danny [Am]boy, I [D]love you [G]so!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
But when ye [G]come, and all the [C]flowers are [G]dying,
If I am [G]dead, as [Em]dead I [Am]well may [D]be,
Ye'll come and [G]find the [G7]place where [C]I am [Am]lying,
And [G]kneel and [Em]say an [Am]Ave there for [D]me;
And I shall [G]hear, tho' [C]soft you tread a[G]bove me,
And all my [Em]grave will [Am]warmer, [D]sweeter be,
For you will [G]bend and [C]tell me [G]that you [Em]love me,
And [G]I shall [Em]sleep in [Am]peace un[D]til you come to [G]me!
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
